      "description": "Hairline frame on white, optional header, hairline-divided key values; no shadow.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-panel\"><div class=\"ds-panel-head\"><h2>Risk model</h2><p>Advisory only.</p></div><dl class=\"ds-kv\"><div><dt>Sensors valid</dt><dd>3 of 5</dd></div><div><dt>Validation</dt><dd class=\"ds-note\">Not commissioned</dd></div></dl></section>",
      "css": ".ds-panel{font-family:Archivo,system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',sans-serif;width:320px;background:#fff;border:1px solid #d6e2ea;border-radius:8px;color:#0f2a3d;} .ds-panel-head{padding:14px 20px;border-bottom:1px solid #e8eff4;} .ds-panel-head h2{margin:0;font-size:15px;font-weight:600;} .ds-panel-head p{margin:2px 0 0;font-size:13px;color:#5b7083;} .ds-kv{margin:0;padding:20px;font-size:14px;} .ds-kv div{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px;padding:10px 0;border-top:1px solid #e8eff4;} .ds-kv div:first-child{border-top:0;padding-top:0;} .ds-kv div:last-child{padding-bottom:0;} .ds-kv dt{color:#3d566a;} .ds-kv dd{margin:0;font-weight:500;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;} .ds-note{color:#a3124b;}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Reading Strip with State Marks",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "reading-cell",
      "description": "Shared-border grid of whole cells: label, tabular value, printed state mark (shape + colour + words).",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-strip\"><div class=\"ds-cell\"><p class=\"ds-lab\">Temperature</p><p class=\"ds-val\">27.4<span>°C</span></p><span class=\"ds-mark ds-ok\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\"><circle cx=\"5\" cy=\"5\" r=\"4\" fill=\"currentColor\"/></svg>Calibrated, within guidance</span></div><div class=\"ds-cell\"><p class=\"ds-lab\">pH</p><p class=\"ds-val\">7.62</p><span class=\"ds-mark ds-trust\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\"><path d=\"M5 1 9 5 5 9 1 5Z\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/></svg>Calibration required</span></div><div class=\"ds-cell\"><p class=\"ds-lab\">ORP</p><p class=\"ds-val ds-empty\">—</p><span class=\"ds-mark ds-off\"><svg viewBox=\"0 0 10 10\"><circle cx=\"5\" cy=\"5\" r=\"3.6\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/></svg>Not reporting</span></div></section>",
      "css": ".ds-strip{font-family:Archivo,system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',sans-serif;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(3,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1px;background:#d6e2ea;border:1px solid #d6e2ea;border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden;width:600px;} .ds-cell{background:#fff;padding:16px 20px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;} .ds-lab{margin:0;font-size:13px;font-weight:500;color:#3d566a;} .ds-val{margin:6px 0 0;font-size:32px;font-weight:600;line-height:1;letter-spacing:-0.025em;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums;color:#0f2a3d;} .ds-val span{margin-left:4px;font-size:16px;font-weight:500;color:#5b7083;} .ds-empty{color:#5b7083;} .ds-mark{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;margin-top:10px;font-size:12px;font-weight:500;line-height:1.375;} .ds-mark svg{width:10px;height:10px;flex-shrink:0;} .ds-ok{color:#1d6b47;} .ds-trust{color:#a3124b;} .ds-off{color:#5b7083;}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Band Chart",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "panel",
      "description": "Signature chart: guidance range as a depth band with dashed contour edges, shoal tint outside, ink line.",
      "html": "<section class=\"ds-chart\"><div class=\"ds-chart-head\"><h3>Temperature (°C)</h3><span>Growth guidance 26–29 °C</span></div><svg viewBox=\"0 0 320 132\" width=\"100%\" height=\"132\" role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Sample temperature trend\"><rect x=\"0\" y=\"0\" width=\"320\" height=\"49.5\" fill=\"#f1e9d2\" opacity=\"0.7\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"99\" width=\"320\" height=\"33\" fill=\"#f1e9d2\" opacity=\"0.7\"/><rect x=\"0\" y=\"49.5\" width=\"320\" height=\"49.5\" fill=\"#e1eef6\"/><line x1=\"0\" x2=\"320\" y1=\"49.5\" y2=\"49.5\" stroke=\"#7aaecb\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><line x1=\"0\" x2=\"320\" y1=\"99\" y2=\"99\" stroke=\"#7aaecb\" stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\"/><path d=\"M0 79 L34 76 L67 73 L101 64 L135 57 L168 45 L202 39 L236 47 L269 61 L303 70 L320 72\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#0f2a3d\" stroke-width=\"1.8\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"/><circle cx=\"168\" cy=\"45\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#a14e06\"/><circle cx=\"202\" cy=\"39\" r=\"2.6\" fill=\"#a14e06\"/></svg><p class=\"ds-chart-note\">Sample data. Shaded band: guidance range; buff: outside range.</p></section>",
      "css": ".ds-chart{font-family:Archivo,system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',sans-serif;width:380px;background:#fff;border:1px solid #d6e2ea;border-radius:8px;padding:14px 16px 12px;color:#0f2a3d;} .ds-chart-head{display:flex;align-items:baseline;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;margin-bottom:8px;} .ds-chart-head h3{margin:0;font-size:14px;font-weight:600;} .ds-chart-head span{font-size:12px;color:#5b7083;} .ds-chart-note{margin:8px 0 0;font-size:12px;line-height:1.625;color:#5b7083;}"
    },
    {
      "name": "Next Line",
      "kind": "custom",
      "refersTo": "next-line-info",
      "description": "Opening wayfinding strip: \"Next\" plus plain-sentence steps linking to the page that resolves them; warn/alarm tints when warranted.",
      "html": "<div class=\"ds-next\"><span class=\"ds-next-k\">Next</span><ul><li>Calibrate the pH probe so readings can be classified. <a href=\"#\">Sensor health</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"ds-next ds-next-warn\"><span class=\"ds-next-k\">Next</span><ul><li>Temperature outside guidance. Check the tank. <a href=\"#\">See details</a></li></ul></div>",
      "css": ".ds-next{font-family:Archivo,system-ui,-apple-system,'Segoe UI',sans-serif;display:flex;gap:12px;width:520px;margin-bottom:8px;padding:12px 16px;border-radius:6px;font-size:14px;line-height:1.625;background:#e1eef6;color:#0f2a3d;} .ds-next-warn{background:#fcf1e1;color:#6b3504;} .ds-next-k{font-weight:600;flex-shrink:0;} .ds-next ul{margin:0;padding:0;list-style:none;} .ds-next a{color:inherit;font-weight:600;white-space:nowrap;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:color-mix(in srgb,currentColor 30%,transparent);text-underline-offset:3px;} .ds-next a:hover{text-decoration-color:currentColor;} .ds-next a:focus-visible{outline:2px solid #1d5d86;outline-offset:2px;}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Hydrographic Chart",
    "overview": "AquaSense reads like a nautical chart of the tank. White is deep water, the ground everything is printed on. Guidance ranges are drawn as pale blue depth bands with dashed contour edges; anything outside them falls on buff shoal tint. Trust is printed in the margin as a chart note: a small mark plus words, magenta when the reading itself cannot be relied on. Ink navy carries text, the rail, and the plotted line. Nothing glows, floats, or tiles.\n\nThe system is dense and quiet. One family (Archivo) ranks everything by size and weight, with tabular numerals wherever numbers line up or update. Structure comes from 1px hairlines and shared-border grids rather than cards with shadows, so the dashboard's reading strip, the public capability grid, and the How-it-works step grid all read as one ruled sheet subdivided into whole cells. Status never relies on colour alone: each state has its own printed shape.\n\nThe public site inherits the same world at a larger scale: ink-on-white editorial headings, the same hairline grids, the navy rail reappearing as the footer and the auth aside, and a static sample band chart standing in for the console.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "White deep-water ground, ink navy text and rail, hairline structure.",
      "Guidance ranges drawn as depth bands with dashed contour edges on every time-series chart.",
      "State shown as a printed mark: shape plus colour plus words.",
      "Magenta is reserved for data-trust notes; red and amber only for real alarms and warnings.",
      "One family, tabular numerals, rank by weight and size, never by case.",
      "Flat at rest; a single soft shadow exists only for things that float over other content."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Chart-Note Rule",
        "body": "Magenta means \"this value is not trustworthy as shown\" and nothing else. It is never a brand accent, link, or decoration.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Real-Alarm Rule",
        "body": "Red and amber appear only when a reported state warrants them (lost connection, outside guidance, active alert, destructive action). Calm screens are ink, white, and blue.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Shoal Rule",
        "body": "Buff marks the water outside a guidance range. If a series has no validated range, draw no band and no shoal; say so in the guidance text instead.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Weight-Not-Case Rule",
        "body": "Hierarchy comes from size and weight. No uppercase labels, no letter-spaced eyebrows above headings.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Rule",
        "body": "Any number that updates live or aligns in a column (readings, meta times, key-value values, schedule times, indices) uses tabular numerals.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Overlay-Only Rule",
        "body": "Panels, cells, buttons and fields have no shadow. If it does not overlap something else, it does not cast one.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do draw every time series with a fixed guidance range as a depth band with dashed contour edges and shoal tint outside it.",
      "Do pair every reading with a State Mark that names its trust state in words and shape, not colour alone.",
      "Do build grids of equal items as shared-border grids (1px gap over the hairline colour) that reflow in whole cells.",
      "Do use tabular numerals for live and aligned numbers.",
      "Do keep calm screens to ink, white, water tints and sounding blue; bring in amber, red or magenta only when the data says so.",
      "Do collapse empty series into a printed sentence rather than drawing empty charts."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't use white cards with coloured icon tiles as KPI grids.",
      "Don't show states as pill badges; use the printed State Mark.",
      "Don't use magenta for anything other than data trust.",
      "Don't put shadows on panels, cells, buttons or fields; the overlay shadow is for floating elements only.",
      "Don't add uppercase or letter-spaced eyebrow labels above headings.",
      "Don't introduce a second typeface."
    ]
  }
}
